lor\" app=\"ikonik\" class=\"path-a3nj6\"></path></svg><div><h4>Licensed &amp; Engineered</h4><div class=\"paragraph-mini\">Florida licensed and insured professionals. Every project is built to code, built to last, and built to impress.</div></div></div></div><div class=\"transformation-actions\"><a href=\"/projects\" class=\"button button-styles w-button\">View All Projects</a><a href=\"/request-estimated\" class=\"button button-styles secundary w-button\">Get a Free Estimate</a></div></div></div></div><div class=\"w-embed w-script\"><!-- Flowbase Booster [Before After Slider] -->\n</div></section><section class=\"mm-proc\"><div class=\"mm-sec-cab\"><h2 class=\"mm-h2\">Our Pool Renovation <span class=\"mm-rot\">Process</span></h2><div class=\"mm-sec-lado\"><p class=\"mm-p\">Our licensed pool contractors manage inspection, demolition, installation, and finishing for renovations that meet Florida safety codes throughout.</p><div class=\"mm-sec-acc\"><a class=\"mm-btn mm-btn--linea\" href=\"#estimate\">Request a Design-Build Project Evaluation</a></div></div></div><div class=\"mm-proc-cuerpo\"><figure class=\"mm-lam-medio mm-proc-medio\" data-mm-pasos-medio=\"\"><img class=\"mm-lam-foto\" src=\"/images/obra/obra-064/pool-remodeling-assessment-old-spa-inspection.avif\" alt=\"Technician inspecting an old tiled spa with a broken brick coping before a pool remodel in Florida\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1200\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><div class=\"mm-lam-pie\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-n=\"01 / 04\" data-t=\"Pool Assessment &amp; Condition Analysis\"></div></figure><ol class=\"mm-pasos\" data-mm-pasos=\"\"><li class=\"mm-paso\"><span class=\"mm-paso-n\">1</span><img class=\"mm-paso-foto\" src=\"/images/obra/obra-064/pool-remodeling-assessment-old-spa-inspection.avif\" alt=\"Technician inspecting an old tiled spa with a broken brick coping before a pool remodel in Florida\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1200\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><h3 class=\"mm-paso-t\">Pool Assessment &amp; Condition Analysis</h3><p>Detailed inspection identifying plaster delamination, structural cracks, equipment aging, circulation inefficiencies, and aesthetic improvements needed. We use underwater camera inspection to assess interior conditions and plan targeted renovations.</p></li><li class=\"mm-paso\"><span class=\"mm-paso-n\">2</span><img class=\"mm-paso-foto\" src=\"/images/obra/obra-053/pool-renovation-travertine-deck-cobalt-tile-spa.avif\" alt=\"French-pattern travertine deck and cobalt tile around a raised spa, materials for a pool renovation in Florida\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1200\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><h3 class=\"mm-paso-t\">Renovation Design &amp; Material Selection</h3><p>Design consultation for modernization including updated finishes, enhanced circulation systems, lighting upgrades, and deck resurfacing options. We present 3D renderings showing before/after transformations.</p></li><li class=\"mm-paso\"><span class=\"mm-paso-n\">3</span><img class=\"mm-paso-foto\" src=\"/images/obra/obra-048/pool-remodeling-crew-at-work-on-drained-pool.avif\" alt=\"Crew cutting block and setting the deck around a drained pool during a pool remodeling project in Florida\" width=\"1260\" height=\"840\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" style=\"object-position:15% 50%\"><h3 class=\"mm-paso-t\">Permits &amp; Project Coordination</h3><p>Acquisition of renovation permits and coordinated scheduling with utility providers. For major renovations, Notice of Commencement filing and ARB re-approval may be required.</p></li><li class=\"mm-paso\"><span class=\"mm-paso-n\">4</span><img class=\"mm-paso-foto\" src=\"/images/obra/obra-064/pool-renovation-new-white-plaster-hand-troweled.avif\" alt=\"Two workers hand-troweling new white plaster in a drained pool with blue waterline tile, pool renovation in Florida\" width=\"1200\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" style=\"object-position:35% 50%\"><h3 class=\"mm-paso-t\">Renovation Execution &amp; System Upgrades</h3><p>Full renovation including surface restoration, equipment replacement, circulation upgrades, and integration of smart automation systems for enhanced functionality and energy efficiency.</p></li></ol></div></section>";
const T6 = "<section class=\"mm-faq\"><div class=\"mm-sec-cab\"><h2 class=\"mm-h2\">Pool Remodeling <span class=\"mm-rot\">FAQs</span></h2><div class=\"mm-sec-lado\"><p class=\"mm-p\">Have questions about pool remodeling in Florida? Our licensed pool contractors answer the top questions from North and South Florida homeowners below.</p></div></div><div class=\"mm-faq-cuerpo\"><div class=\"mm-faq-lista\"><details class=\"mm-faq-item\"><summary><h3>Why remodel a pool in Florida?</h3><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"mm-faq-r\"><p>Pool remodeling improves efficiency, safety, appearance, and long-term property value, making Florida pools significantly easier to enjoy. Licensed under CPC1460562 and CPC1461119, Mr. &amp; Mrs. Outdoor Living handles the full scope — from structural inspection through final finish application.</p></div></details><details class=\"mm-faq-item\"><summary><h3>What energy savings can pool upgrades provide?</h3><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"mm-faq-r\"><p>It depends on the equipment being replaced and how the pool is run, so we do not quote a percentage. Variable-speed pumps are the biggest lever: they move the same water at lower speeds for most of the day, and Florida law (section 553.909, Florida Statutes) already requires residential pool pumps of 1 horsepower or more to run at two or more speeds. In a complete remodel we size the pump, filtration and low-voltage LED lighting to the renovated pool as one system, instead of swapping parts one at a time.</p></div></details><details class=\"mm-faq-item\"><summary><h3>How long does a pool remodel take in Florida?</h3><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"mm-faq-r\"><p>It depends on the scope: an interior refinish with new tile moves faster than a remodel that rebuilds the shell, replaces the equipment and redoes the deck. We assess the pool first and give you the schedule for your scope in writing, together with the fixed project price, before any demolition starts. Permit review and inspections are part of that schedule, and we coordinate them.</p></div></details><details class=\"mm-faq-item\"><summary><h3>Can features be added during a pool renovation?</h3><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"mm-faq-r\"><p>Yes. Pool renovations are an ideal time to add spas, tanning ledges, waterfalls, LED lighting, and smart automation systems. Our licensed pool contractors manage the permitting and installation of all additions alongside the renovation work, keeping your project coordinated and on schedule.</p></div></details><details class=\"mm-faq-item\"><summary><h3>Do you offer financing options for outdoor projects?</h3><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"mm-faq-r\"><p>Yes. We connect Florida homeowners with lending partners, and the order matters: you get the scope of the renovation and a fixed project price in writing first, and only then review how to pay for it. Approval and terms come from the lender.</p></div></details><details class=\"mm-faq-item\"><summary><h3>How much does a complete pool remodel cost in North Florida?</h3><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"mm-faq-r\"><p>There is no single number: a remodel is priced from the condition of the shell, the finish and tile you choose, the equipment being replaced and the deck work around it. Our estimator walks you through those choices, and you get a fixed project price in writing before any demolition starts.</p></div></details><details class=\"mm-faq-item\"><summary><h3>Does a pool remodel need a permit in Florida?</h3><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"mm-faq-r\"><p>Usually, yes. Work that touches the structure, plumbing, electrical, equipment or the safety barrier is permitted and inspected under the Florida Building Code; resurfacing alone is treated differently by different jurisdictions. We confirm the scope with the building department and pull the permits under our license.</p></div></details><details class=\"mm-faq-item\"><summary><h3>What is included in a complete pool remodel?</h3><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"mm-faq-r\"><p>An assessment of the shell and plumbing, then the scope you choose: interior finish, waterline tile and coping, equipment and lighting, a spa added or rebuilt, deck resurfacing or replacement, and a code-compliant barrier, finished with start-up and a walk-through of the new equipment.</p></div></details></div><div class=\"mm-faq-lado\"><figure class=\"mm-lam-medio mm-faq-medio\"><img class=\"mm-lam-foto\" src=\"/images/images/pool-remodeling-4/custom-pool-remodeling-contractors-florida-04.jpg\" alt=\"Long lap pool with a raised spa and a wide paver deck beside an open lawn, pool renovation in Florida\" width=\"1250\" height=\"933\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></figure><div class=\"mm-faq-accion\"><a class=\"mm-btn\" href=\"#estimate\">Request a Design-Build Project Evaluation</a><div class=\"mm-datos\"><a class=\"mm-dato\" href=\"tel:+13527403361\"><span class=\"mm-dato-rot\">North Florida</span><span class=\"mm-dato-val\">+1 (352) 740-3361</span></a><a class=\"mm-dato\" href=\"tel:+19549137112\"><span class=\"mm-dato-rot\">South Florida</span><span class=\"mm-dato-val\">+1 (954) 913-7112</span></a></div></div></div></div></section><section class=\"testimonial-section\"><div class=\"w-layout-blockcontainer container w-container\"><div data-w-id=\"74852c7c-aeb3-35a7-5cf1-44f4ce6ecae5\" class=\"header-reviews\"><div class=\"label\">TESTIMONIALS</div><h2 class=\"white\">What Our Clients Say About Mr &amp; Mrs Outdoor Living</h2><p>Read testimonials from Florida clients enjoying safer, more beautiful pools after professional renovation by our licensed pool remodeling contractors.</p></div>";
